## Auth & identity

- **Sign-in:** Supabase email/password only; no OAuth (Google/Facebook). Users with an email must have **`email_confirmed_at`** set (confirmed via Supabase email) before the app treats them as signed in; otherwise they see **INVALID EMAIL OR PASSWORD** and the session is cleared. **Passwords are never stored** in `localStorage` or auth backup cookies — only Supabase session tokens. Legacy local-only sign-in/bootstrap paths were removed.
- **Build-a-Wig entry (signed-in only):** Unit PDP **CUSTOMIZE IN BUILD-A-WIG**, mobile menu **BUILD-A-WIG**, **cart dropdown** and **shopping bag** **EDIT IN BUILD-A-WIG** require sign-in: **`BuildAWigFeatureSignInModal`** (`FORGOT SOMETHING?` / “You must sign in to access this feature.”). **`returnTo`** for cart/bag edit is the product-specific **`/build-a-wig/.../edit`** route (localStorage for **`editingCartItem`** is set before the modal). **Shopping bag `+ LIST`** (add to wishlist list) uses the same modal when signed out; **`returnTo`** is the current bag URL. **`ShopMobileMenuShopTab`** accepts optional **`onBuildAWigRequiresSignIn`** + **`isSignedInForBuildAWig`**. After sign-in from the hub, **`?bawMenu=1`** opens the menu on **`/build-a-wig/noir`** (strip-once `useEffect`); booking **`BookingFlowLayout`** uses the same gate for **`/build-a-wig/noir`**. **View mode** (`/build-a-wig/view/…` only; legacy **`/build-a-wig/try/…`** redirects): footer **VIEW SUBSCRIPTIONS** + hub **SAVE SLAY CARD** for signed-out, standard, and premium members; option sub-pages use **SAVE SELECTION**. Member customize/edit routes use commerce footers (**ADD TO BAG** / **CONFIRM SELECTION** / **CUSTOMIZE IN BUILD-A-WIG**). Legacy **`/build-a-wig`** redirects — guests → **`/build-a-wig/view`**, signed-in → **`/build-a-wig/noir`**.
- **Sign out from the menu toggle:** Use **`signOutAppAndSupabaseSession()`** (`adminAuth.ts`) — **`markManualSignOutInProgress`**, **`supabase.auth.signOut()`**, **`clearAppAuth()`**, and **`signInStateChanged`**. Clearing only **`localStorage`** left the Supabase session in **`sb-*-auth-token`** + cookies, so **`main.tsx`** **`bootstrapAuthBeforeRender`** re-applied the user on the next navigation.
- **Shopping bag (`/bag`) and checkout:** **`CommerceRouteGuard`** always allows **`/bag`**, **`/checkout`**, **`/checkout/bookings`**, and **`/checkout/gift-card`** so guests can view the bag and pay without a Supabase session. **`CartDropdown`**: when the dropdown closes, it still mounts **`BuildAWigFeatureSignInModal`** so **EDIT IN BUILD-A-WIG** can open the gate after **`onClose()`**. On **`/bag`**, **`BuildAWigFeatureSignInModal`** instances for **EDIT IN BUILD-A-WIG** and **`+ LIST`** are rendered via **`createPortal(..., document.body)`** so overlays sit above page content (same stacking idea as cart).
- **Admin list:** `src/utils/adminAuth.ts`. Default admin emails include `kateenaarmstrong@gmail.com`, `admin@frontalslayer.com`, `kateena.armstrong@frontalslayer.com`. Env overrides: `VITE_ADMIN_EMAILS` (frontend), `ADMIN_EMAILS` (Vercel API). When set, env list is used (include all desired admins, e.g. Supabase emails for each operator).
- **Admin features:** Access to `/admin/*`, “Sync my account” in Account → Settings, Concierge card for founder-privileged admin and premium. Sync uses `POST /api/admin/sync-profile` with email + password (Supabase credentials). **Admin founder** (same as founder-privileged admin): `kateenaarmstrong@gmail.com` — `FOUNDER_PRIVILEGED_ADMIN_EMAIL` / `isAyoteenzAdminAccount` / `isAdminFounderAccount` in `adminAuth.ts`. **ADMIN: FOUNDER** on Account → Profile (tap → `/admin/dashboard`), tier/subscription test toggles, mock loyalty/vouchers, merged mock clients in admin UI. **Admin Meetings demo consults** for the founder account: **ORDER #331** (`adminFounderDemoConsultMeetingOrder331`, id **`demo-baw-consult-order-331`**, 2:00 PM), **ORDER #340** (`adminFounderDemoConsultMeetingOrder340`, **`demo-baw-consult-order-340`**, 3:30 PM — custom / gallery inspo path), **ORDER #341** (`adminFounderDemoConsultMeetingOrder341`, **`demo-baw-consult-order-341`**, 4:45 PM — alternate unit / AI preview path). Merged **after** mock/API/local rows when **`isAdminEmail(currentUser)`** so backend rows cannot replace them; **`listAggregatedAdminMeetingsForClientDetails`** uses the same rule. Dated **first day of the hub’s visible calendar month**. Matching **Account → Orders** rows: **ORDER #331** (COMPLETE + offer snapshot) is injected into **past** when missing; **ORDER #340** and **#341** are **PROCESSING** with **no** pre-built quote/snapshot and are injected into **active** when missing (end-to-end **Send offer** testing; see `mergeFounderAdminConsultOrder331Demo` in `orders/page.tsx`). Consult list search includes **`metadata.orderNumber`** and meeting **`id`**. **Delete account:** only `PROTECTED_FROM_ACCOUNT_DELETION_EMAIL` (same Gmail by default) is blocked client + server; `ayoteenz@yahoo.com` and all other users can delete if the API succeeds (`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` required on Vercel).

---

## Key flows

- **Account / Concierge:** Priority messages, order tracking, Slay Challenge (6‑month cycles, reward selection), Special Offer (configurable via Admin → Marketing; $40 off, 60‑day countdown), Free Gift, Birthday Gift. Founder-privileged admin can override Slay Challenge stage for testing.
- **Account → Rewards (premium chart) + subscription checkout:** The premium comparison chart and **CONFIRM SUBSCRIPTION** live on **Account → Rewards** at **`/account/rewards`** (`src/pages/account/membership/page.tsx`). Confirming navigates to **`/checkout/upgrade`** with the tier in `localStorage` (`subscriptionUpgrade`). **Subscribe with card (Stripe)** appears only on **`/checkout/upgrade`** (`src/pages/checkout/page.tsx`), not on Rewards, when **`GET /api/stripe/membership-available`** is **`available: true`** and the user has a **Supabase** session (`getAccessToken()`). Stripe success returns to **`/checkout/upgrade?stripe=success`**, then the app syncs profile and routes to Rewards. There is no separate nav item labeled “Membership.”
- **Admin / Marketing:** Special-offer config at **`/admin/marketing`** (nav: "ADMIN > MARKETING"). Page: product, length, density, texture, lace, hairline (incl. LAGOS + PEAK), color, styling (incl. Bangs combos), add-ons (dropdown with all combinations: NONE, single, BLEACH + PLUCK, etc., via `ADDON_COMBO_OPTIONS`), thumbnail, start date. All dropdown panels use `max-h-48 overflow-y-auto` for scrolling. Save Config and RANDOMIZE (red text) below card; RANDOMIZE fills all options with valid random values. **Persistence:** Save writes `specialOfferAdminConfig` to localStorage and upserts the same JSON to Supabase `app_config` key `special_offer_admin` via **`PUT /api/admin/special-offer-config`** (admin session). Concierge and the admin editor load from **`GET /api/special-offer-config`** first, then fall back to localStorage. **Newsletter tab:** After **SPECIAL OFFERS** — HTML email to clients with `notificationNewsletter` opt-in (Account → Settings); templates + recipient multi-select; **`POST /api/admin/newsletter-send`** (admin session) sends via **Resend** when **`RESEND_API_KEY`** (+ optional **`NEWSLETTER_FROM_EMAIL`**) are set on the server; up to 100 recipients per request (UI chunks larger sends). **Transactional email:** Branded HTML templates in **`api/_lib/email/`** — server-only **`sendEmail({ templateType, recipientEmail, subject?, variables? })`** via Resend; assets in Supabase Storage bucket **`email-assets`** (`npm run email:upload-assets`); **`POST /api/email/send`** (admin or **`EMAIL_SEND_SECRET`**) for previews/sends. Wired triggers: Stripe order confirm, membership welcome, affiliate pending/approve/deny, branded password reset, meeting alerts. See **`docs/EMAIL_SYSTEM.md`**.
- **Cart / bag / wishlist line typography:** Product copy (script name, red RAW, CAP SIZE, price, meta) uses **fixed-height layers** — `CartLineProductTextStack` + `CartLineTextLayer` (`src/components/cart/CartLineProductTextStack.tsx`, `src/utils/cartLineProductLayers.ts`) — with symmetric **2px** vertical padding per row so **NOIR** (22px name) sets rhythm and other units align without per-product `marginTop` hacks. Wishlist uses `WishlistLineProductTextStack` / `WishlistItemCapSizeLine` (cap in `slot="cap"`). Legacy spacing helpers in `cartCapSizeLineMargin.ts` remain for spec checks / normalization (`normalizeCartLineProductName`).
- **Storefront inventory (wig units):** Admin **remaining units** (`getDepletedInventory` in `adminRevenueStats.ts` from `userOrders_*` + optional `adminInventoryOverride`) drive shopper **sold-out** UI for the six unit SKUs (**NOIR**, **BLANCO**, **SOFT WAVE**, **BEACH WAVE**, **SOFT CURL**, **OCEAN CURL**). Shared helpers: `src/utils/productInventoryAvailability.ts` (`isWigUnitSoldOut`, `getLineItemStockStatus`, `attachStockStatusToLineItem`); `useProductInventorySnapshot` + `ProductInventorySync` refresh cart/wishlist `stockStatus` on focus/cart/inventory events. Sold-out **cart/bag/wishlist** lines: **red** `OUT OF STOCK`, price **strikethrough** (`WigLineStockPrice`). **Unit PDP** when sold out: price shown **without** strikethrough (`WigProductPriceDisplay` `soldOutPriceTreatment="normal"`); **ADD TO BAG** → disabled **OUT OF STOCK**; **CUSTOMIZE** → **NOTIFY ME WHEN AVAILABLE** + `StockNotifyModal` (`unitStockNotify.ts` waitlist + Account → Alerts row when email has an account). Restock fires **back-in-stock** account alert via `processUnitStockNotifyWaitlistOnInventoryUpdate` on inventory events.
- **Cart / Wishlist:** Stored in localStorage (global and per-user keys). Synced to backend on sign-in/sync where applicable. **BCF bundle-deal** lines (`bcfBundleDeal`): in the **shopping bag** they use the same controls as **A/C** booking lines — **QTY** label + **×** remove only (no **+ LIST**, no ± stepper, no **SAVE FOR LATER**). If the user **no longer qualifies** for premium-gated features (`isPremiumMemberForGatedFeatures` in `premiumMemberAccess.ts` — active premium subscription and/or **BLACK** spend tier), **`isPremiumGatedCartLine`** rows are **removed**: **bundle-deal**, all **`booking-appointment`** (hair installs), and **`booking-consult`** with **`bookingTier === 'premium'`** (standard consults remain). Same strip runs on **`cartItems`** / **`savedForLater`** load, **`signInStateChanged`** / **`focus`** (`applyStripIneligibleBcfBundleDealsToAllStoredCarts` in **`App.tsx`**), **`CartDropdown`**, **`/checkout`**, **`/checkout/summary`** (localStorage fallback), bag **`loadCartItems` / `loadSavedForLater`**. **`MOVE TO BAG`** from saved is blocked for any **`isPremiumGatedCartLine`** when not premium. **Booking:** **`/booking/premium/consultation`** (and **`/consult`**) — **add to bag** is blocked with **`ConfirmationModal`** unless **`isPremiumMemberForGatedFeatures()`** (same pattern as **`/booking/premium/appointment`** and **`/booking/appointment`**); SHOP menu routes non-premium users to standard **`/booking/consultation`** via **`bookingMenuUsesPremiumPaths()`** in **`bookingMemberRoutes.ts`**. **Build-a-wig:** options under **PREMIUM MEMBERSHIP OPTIONS** (lace, texture, color, hairline, styling, add-ons) require the same gate — hub **`handleOptionSelect`** shows upgrade modal; sub-routes use **`useBuildWigPremiumMembershipStepGate`** (`src/hooks/useBuildWigPremiumMembershipStepGate.tsx`). Categories list: **`buildWigPremiumOptions.ts`**.
- **Checkout order strip (shared with cart dropdown):** Horizontal cart tiles on **`/checkout`** and **`/checkout/summary`** use **`src/utils/checkoutOrderStripDisplay.ts`** — same thumbnail sizes/nudges and title/red line as **`CartDropdown`** (BCF shop lines, unit wigs, gift card, membership tiers). **A/C** = internal shorthand for **appointment + consult** booking cart lines (`booking-appointment`, `booking-consult`); titles **BOOKING** / **CONSULT**, badge thumbs **66px** in an **88px** slot (not the large header badge size).
- **Consult quote checkout codes:** Admin-sent **`CONSULT-*`** codes are validated with **`POST /api/checkout/validate-consult-code`** (signed-in owner, not expired, not redeemed); discount applies to non–booking cart subtotal on **`/checkout`** (not **`/checkout/bookings`**). After a successful order, **`POST /api/checkout/redeem-consult-code`** sets **`consult_quotes.redeemed_at`**. Migration **`20260403140000_consult_quotes_redeemed_at.sql`** adds **`redeemed_at`**. **Account → Orders** archived consult **VIEW OFFER** opens **`ConsultOfferClaimModal`** (thumbnail, breakdown, 72h timer, claim → bag + checkout auto-apply); **`markConsultOrderCompleteAfterQuoteSent`** can persist **`consultOfferSnapshot`** on the order for local/offline. **Admin meeting edits:** **`POST /api/admin/meeting-client-alert`** appends a client **notifications** item (reschedule vs cancel); **`AdminMeetingsHub`** uses **RESCHEDULE** / **CANCEL** buttons after **`PATCH`** notes. **Admin Meetings → Send offer:** dropdown option lists render in a **fixed-position portal** to **`document.body`** (high z-index) so lists are not clipped by the main card; default unit preview uses **`ordersPageUnitThumbnailSrcFromUnitKey`** in **`accountReviewProductThumbnail.ts`** (same 2D asset paths as Account → Orders wig list thumbs); optional **CUSTOM IMAGE:** picker (**`OrderFormFilePicker`**, same as order authorization; admin send-offer uses **`hideInlinePreview`** so only the **~122px** preview thumb shows, not a second large image in the picker). Session draft stores manual upload separately; **`localStorage`** key **`bawAdminConsultOfferSavedThumbnails`** maps **unit + length + density + color + hairline + styling + parting** (`partSelection`) **+ add-ons** (sorted) only → **`data:`** URL when admin taps **SAVE SELECTION** (after choosing a file). **STYLING** category adds **PARTING:** (**MIDDLE** / **LEFT** / **RIGHT**) below the styling salon row; **`partSelection`** is stored on **`consult_quotes.selections`** / cart (**$0** **PARTING** line omitted from persisted price breakdown + UI list). Price breakdown amounts use a leading **`+`** for positive lines (including **UNIT**).
- **Consult-only checkout orders** (`bookingFlowType: 'consult'`): **`PLACED` → `PROCESSING`** after **2 hours** from **`placedAt`** (`CONSULT_PLACED_TO_PROCESSING_MS` in **`consultOrderLifecycle.ts`**); **`COMPLETE`** after **72h** from **`placedAt`** (same file). **Orders / confirm / Concierge** consult tracking bar: **`consultDigitalOrderTrackingBarFillPct`** in **`digitalOrderFulfillment.ts`** — **`PLACED`**: ~**10% → 30%** over the first **2h**; **`PROCESSING`**: **30% → 100%** over the remaining **70h** to the 72h window; **`COMPLETE`**: **100%**.
- **Style analysis (consult add-on + PSA selfie):** **Optional** style analysis add-on on **`/booking/consultation`** — when selected, client uploads **selfie** inside the chosen 1- or 4-pick panel plus **hair inspo**; **1 / 4** comparison options → **$20 / $60** (bundled into consult checkout total with **$40** deposit). Skip add-on = **$40 deposit only** (no selfie). **Consult pipeline:** `POST /api/consult-style-analysis-generate` — preferred path is **manual specs** (`manualSpecs` / `inspoSpecs`) selected for the submitted hair inspo image; OpenAI vision spec mapping remains fallback only. Fal populates the same **1 pick** (`IMG_2554`) / **4 pick** (`IMG_2549`) hairstyle analysis templates (`six_month` / `twelve_month`). **Consult prompt rule:** both 1-pick and 4-pick templates must preserve the photographed inspo hairstyle as the visual source of truth (length, bangs/fringe, curl/crimp/wave pattern, part, silhouette, color saturation); BAW spec labels/refs are guardrails only and must not collapse unique inspo styling into generic layers/none or over-long hair. Long-hair drape should be **one-forward-shoulder**: one forward chest cascade on one side, visible hair routed behind the opposite shoulder/down the back, no equal thick forward curtains, and no all-hair-on-one-shoulder pile. **Consult post-process:** force the bottom fade pass, then use the original subtle mirror reflection below that fade; avoid extra client-panel chrome/bottom-overflow template restoration unless a separate artifact-specific fix is designed. **4 pick:** TOP MATCH = inspo on client; MATCH 02–04 = same inspo hairstyle in **3** alternate colors. **Admin debug:** `/tools/hairstyle-analysis` hair consult tiers show selfie + hair inspo + **Manual specs for this hair inspo**; those TOP MATCH picker values are sent as manual specs. **PSA** premium-only **`FIND MY BEST LOOKS`** — ranked unit upsells; results deliver **within 24 hours**. **Template cards (catalog manifest):** `POST /api/hairstyle-analysis-generate`. Admin Tools debug: **1 pick**, **4 pick**, **hair consult 1 pick**, **hair consult 4 pick**. See **`docs/STYLE_ANALYSIS.md`**.
- **`/checkout/bookings`:** Nav crumb **CHECKOUT > BOOKING** (singular). Checkout logic treats **bookings-only** carts like **digital** for **shipping** (no ship address / calculator / method / delivery UI, no tax or loyalty points on that subtotal, billing required, package protection skipped) via **`checkoutSkipsShipping`** and **`isBookingsOnlyCheckoutState`** in **`utils/bookingCheckout.ts`**.
- **`/checkout/gift-card`:** Isolated gift-card checkout (bag filtered to gift lines). Gift cards use the **digital** 3-stage fulfillment timeline only — **no** order authorization form (forms are for hair-related units / BCF bundles, closures, and frontals only).
- **Orders:** Active/past orders per user; tracking stages with progress. Mock/test orders for admin (e.g. Kateena) for demos.
- **Admin → Pending (cross-device when Supabase + migration applied):** Server tables **`pending_order_forms`**, **`pending_affiliate_submissions`**, **`pending_review_supplemental`**, plus **`reviews`** rows with **`status = pending`**. Admin UI loads **`GET /api/admin/pending-queue`** (service role) and **`PATCH`** approve/decline updates DB + **`profiles.user_submitted_reviews`**, **`profiles.affiliate_submitted_content`**, **`profiles.signed_order_forms`**, **`profiles.review_supplemental_overlay`** (catalog/mock review ids), and **`orders`** where applicable. Clients POST **`/api/client/submissions`** (Bearer) for order form, review, supplemental media, affiliate batch; then **`syncProfileFromApi`** mirrors profile JSON into localStorage (**`clientPendingServerSync`**). **Migrations:** run **`20260413120000_pending_admin_queues.sql`** and **`20260414100000_profiles_review_supplemental_overlay.sql`** in Supabase SQL Editor. Without migration or session token, app falls back to prior **localStorage-only** mock queues.
- **Sync:** Profile/orders/cart/wishlist sync via **`syncAllFromApi`** / **`syncProfileWithToken`** (Bearer session to `/api/admin/sync-profile`). Admin email must be in `VITE_ADMIN_EMAILS` and `ADMIN_EMAILS`. No password is sent from the browser.
- **Lounge TV (lobby salon):** Play on lobby opens **`LoungeTvOverlay`** (curtains, CRT static, hand/remote) — **room chrome unchanged**; only the **black TV panel** content was restructured (2026-07). **Nav tabs:** FEATURED, LEARN, EXPLORE, LIVE, LIBRARY. Weekly items are **`LoungeContentPack`** metadata (`src/components/lounge/loungeTvContentPack.ts`) — video + article + transcript + checklist + products + ticket fields; placeholder seed includes **CUTTING YOUR LACE** (BOTH, 8 MIN / 4 MIN, Lace Mastery, free preview). **UI:** streaming rows/cards (`LoungeTvContentPackCard`, `LoungeTvContentRow`), Featured homepage rows, Learn lesson hub (WATCH EPISODE / READ GUIDE), premium article + video detail views, Live placeholders, Library sections (continue/saved/unlocked/etc. via `src/utils/loungeTvLibrary.ts`). Admin **`lounge_tv_admin`** placements migrate legacy `brand` / `slay-tips` / `watch-learn` / `academy` tab keys to new tabs. Tiles still resolve via **`resolveLoungeTvTiles`** for CMS overrides. **Watch player:** **`LoungeTvWatchLearnPlayer`**. **Ticket-gated thumbs:** blur + centered **`loungeTvLockedThumbnailOverlayLabel`** copy (no lock icons / red corner badges); unlocked library access = crisp thumbnail. **\*NEW\*** label only (no blur by itself). **Session:** open state restores only on **full reload** while route is **`/lobby/lounge`** (`readLoungeTvOpenRestoreAfterReload`); leaving the lounge slide or lobby clears the flag and collapses TV; **X only** closes (no backdrop/Escape). **Capture guard:** **`useLoungeTvCaptureGuard`** + **`LoungeTvContentProtection`**. **Phase 2 streaming catalog (2026-07):** metadata-only evolution — **`loungeTvStreamingCatalog.ts`**, **`loungeTvStreamingTypes.ts`**, **`loungeTvStreamSeriesData.ts`** / **`loungeTvStreamSeries.ts`** (Season/Episode), **`loungeTvCollections.ts`**, **`loungeTvPersonalizedRails.ts`**, **`loungeTvArtwork.ts`**, **`loungeTvContentStatus.ts`**, **`loungeTvStreamingMeta.ts`** (hydrate packs), **`loungeTvPsaHostMessages.ts`**, **`loungeTvFilterIndex.ts`**, **`loungeTvCardEnhancements.ts`**, **`loungeTvSeriesProgress.ts`**; skippable PSA intro; watch progress % + resume in player; card progress bar / premiere ribbon / poster roles — UI architecture unchanged. **DRM deferred** (see MEMORY 2026-05-29).
- **Admin → THE STUDIO:** **studio os** platform — layered architecture: **`src/studio-os-core/`** (reusable platform logic) → **`src/workspaces/`** (registry + brand implementations) → **`src/workspaces/frontal-slayer/`** (first production workspace). Deprecated shim: **`src/studio-os/index.ts`** re-exports core. Platform identity in `studio-os-core/config/platform.ts`. Entry **`/admin/studio-os`** — workspace picker; default Workspace **FRONTAL SLAYER**. Placeholder workspaces: **`sandbox/`**, **`future-brand/`**, **`future-client/`**. Registry injection via `configureWorkspaceRegistry()`; **`AdminStudioWorkspaceGuard`** loads `workspaces` + **`WorkspaceProvider`** for **`/admin/studio/*`** and **`/admin/studio-os/*` only** — **`AdminGuard`** is auth-only (dashboard never waits on Milestone seeds). Docs: **`docs/studio-os/architecture.md`**, **`workspace-system.md`**, **`core-vs-workspace.md`**, **`docs/frontal-slayer/workspace-implementation.md`**. **`/admin/studio`** redirects to **Mission Control**; **Studio Overview** (grouped nav) at **`/admin/studio/overview`**; legacy hub at **`/admin/studio/hub`**; Executive Command Center at **`/admin/studio/executive-command-center`**. Shared Studio shell: **`AdminStudioLayout`** + **`adminStudioNavigation.ts`** (OVERVIEW / CREATE / VISUALS / PRODUCTION / DISTRIBUTION / INTELLIGENCE / LEGACY / SETTINGS), breadcrumbs, back-to-overview link, **`AdminStudioModuleCard`**. **Social Publishing** (`/admin/studio/social-accounts`) — official OAuth connectors (Meta Graph Instagram/Facebook, TikTok Content Posting API, Pinterest API, X API when available); tokens encrypted server-side only; Distribution Network pack **SOCIAL** tab; admin approval required before publish; **`socialPublishingStudioService`**; migration **`20260704120000_studio_social_publishing.sql`**; see **`docs/STUDIO_SOCIAL_PUBLISHING.md`**. **Legacy System** (`/admin/studio/legacy-system`) — permanent memory & living museum: editorial landing cards, The Museum with archives, Hall of Fame, Studio Awards, talent careers, Vault of Firsts, time capsules, timeline, founder journal (founder-only), **`legacySystemStudioService`**. **Asset Director** (`/admin/studio/asset-director`) — **visual asset management** (Milestone 14): 21:9 hero, gallery/list modes, filters, bulk actions, quick preview; studio detail bundles (versions, videos, cameras, lighting, props, talent portraits, wardrobe views, expressions, poses, materials, relationships, moodboard masonry, version timeline, health cards; metadata collapsed); Content Pack visual picker; placeholder only — **`adminStudioAssetDirectorVisual.ts`**, **`assetDirectorStudioService`**. **Production Builder** (`/admin/studio/production-builder`, optional **`?packId=`**) — **visual production assembly** (Milestone 14.5): three-column workspace (asset library · scene builder · inspector), multi-scene shot builder with drag-reorder, auto prompt assembly from approved assets, output types, brand aspect previews, department status bar, templates, save/duplicate/favorite/archive/version history, **Build Production** demo outputs; syncs scene selection to Content Pack asset store; **OPEN IN PRODUCTION BUILDER** on pack detail; **🎬 ENTER DIRECTOR MODE** CTA; placeholder — **`adminStudioProductionBuilderDemo.ts`**, **`productionBuilderStudioService`**. **Director Mode** (`/admin/studio/director-mode`, **`?draftId=`** from Production Builder) — **cinematic rehearsal** (Milestone 15): four-zone control room (timeline · cinema preview · director controls · production console), live storyboard, script/shot list, camera & lighting simulation, talent/voice/music/graphics controls, readiness score, AI rehearsal simulation, director notes, client preview, snapshots, emergency checklist gating **Generate Production**; **Ask Executive AI Director** panel; syncs to Production Builder draft + Content Packs; placeholder — **`adminStudioDirectorModeDemo.ts`**, **`directorModeStudioService`**. **Executive AI Director** (`/admin/studio/executive-ai-director`) — **strategic intelligence advisor** (Milestone 16): Today's Brief, creative intelligence (searchable), production coaching, brand compliance, prompt review (0–100), executive scorecard, performance forecasts (labeled estimates), trend signal plugins (internal only), recommendations, A/B strategy, content gaps, workspace memory (append-only), executive + production timelines, executive chat; analyzes Production Builder drafts; placeholder — **`adminStudioExecutiveAiDirectorDemo.ts`**, **`executiveAiDirectorStudioService`**. **Campaign Orchestrator** (`/admin/studio/campaign-orchestrator`) — **operational launch planner** (Milestone 17): one business objective → full execution plan; 5-step wizard (identity · audience · schedule · creative direction · generate), 16 campaign types + reusable blueprints, visual timeline, auto task generation with department assignment + dependency chains, Executive AI Director pre-production review, dashboard (progress/readiness/risk, deliverables, approvals, automation rules, what-if scenarios, resource view, smart recommendations with reasoning); human approval gates at production/generation/publishing/scheduling/distribution — never auto-executes; placeholder — **`adminStudioCampaignOrchestratorDemo.ts`**, **`adminStudioCampaignOrchestratorPlan.ts`**, **`campaignOrchestratorStudioService`**. **Mission Control** (`/admin/studio/mission-control`) — **workspace executive HQ** (Milestone 18): landing page after workspace selection; modular dashboard (workspace header · executive brief · mission overview hero · active missions · docked Executive AI Director · department grid · mission timeline · executive calendar · approval center · business health scorecards · quick actions · workspace memory · sticky live activity feed); mission search + smart notifications; placeholder — **`adminStudioMissionControlDemo.ts`**, **`missionControlStudioService`**. **`/admin/studio`** redirects to Mission 