## Conventions

- **Explanations for this product owner:** When walking through setup, architecture, or technical steps, assume the reader may **not** be developer-savvy yet. Prefer **plain language**, short steps, analogies (e.g. shopping list, photo album, hired artist), and **Windows-friendly** notes where relevant; introduce jargon only when needed and define it in one line. Put long checklists in **`docs/`** when appropriate so the chat stays scannable.

- **Desktop perspective panel mapping:** Tilted/acrylic/holographic surfaces use **4-corner quads** (image-normalized 0–1) via **`<PerspectivePanel id="…">`** (`src/components/perspective-panel/`). Central defs: **`src/constants/perspectivePanelConfig.ts`** (reception-left/center/right, curator-tablet, checkout-tablet, signin-tablet, tv-lounge-screen, psa-hologram-screen, extensions-boutique-wall). Warp math: **`PerspectivePanelHost`** + **`quadPerspectiveTransform.ts`** + **`desktopRoomCoverLayout.ts`**. **Debug:** set **`window.PANEL_DEBUG = true`** in DevTools (or **`?panelDebug=1`**) — crimson dashed polygons, draggable corners, floating **PANEL DEBUG** toolbar (select panel, edit all, reset, copy/import JSON, save to **`localStorage.perspectivePanelMap`**). Export approved JSON into config for production; do not rely on localStorage alone. Legacy rect-only **`?panelDebug=1`** alignment for Penthouse account panels remains under **`src/components/desktop-panel-debug/`** until migrated.
- **Desktop room overlays (cover-locked):** NO TEXT desktop heroes are **1915×821** with **`object-fit: cover`** + **`center top`** (`DesktopZoneRoomScene`). **All** overlays on those rooms must use **image-normalized coordinates (0–1)** mapped through **`desktopRoomCoverLayout.ts`** — not raw viewport `%` or `vw`. Flat rects may use **`DesktopRoomCoverRectAnchor`**; perspective surfaces use **`PerspectivePanel`**.
- **Lobby (home) nav:** Neon logo (center) and **Products** (neon-products) → `/home/shop`. Tools (neon-tools) → `/home/tools`. Lounge carousel logo → `/shop/units`. Implemented in `src/pages/lobby/page.tsx` (Products uses the full neon asset as the tap target, not a shifted overlay).
- **App default route:** `/` and the index route use **`HomeLandingRedirect`** (`App.tsx`) — **premium** members (subscription and/or BLACK tier) → **`/lobby`**; **standard** members and guests → **`/home/shop`**. Direct navigation to `/home/shop` or `/lobby` is unchanged.
- **Paths:** Pages under `src/pages/` (e.g. `account/`, `account/settings/`, `account/concierge/`, `admin/`). Shared components in `src/components/`, utils in `src/utils/`.
- **State:** React `useState`/`useEffect`; persistent data in localStorage (`currentUser`, `registeredUsers`, cart, wishlist, per-user keys). Supabase session for server-backed data.
- **API:** Base URL from `VITE_API_BASE`; routes in `api/` (e.g. `api/admin/sync-profile`, `api/delete-account`). CORS and JSON error responses on API routes. **Checkout hardening (partial):** `POST /api/checkout/quote` recomputes USD from cart **identities** (booking, consult, simple unit names) and can return `chargeCurrency` / `chargeAmountMinor` via `api/_lib/pricing/fxRates.ts`; `GET /api/fx/rates` exposes the FX table; `POST /api/stripe/create-product-payment-intent` charges in the shopper’s `chargeCurrency` when the cart is fully server-resolvable; webhook `payment_intent.succeeded` can append an order. Details: `docs/CHECKOUT_SERVER_QUOTE.md`. Full checkout subtotal (tax/shipping/vouchers) is still client-side for display; PI amount is server line-item USD converted to charge currency.
- **Docs:** Project docs in `docs/` (e.g. `ADMIN_SYNC_SUPABASE_EMAIL_WALKTHROUGH.md`, `DELETE_ACCOUNT_API_WALKTHROUGH.md`). **Profiles:** Exact Supabase `profiles` columns and how they map to the API and app (name, photo, socials, birthday, rewards) are in `docs/PROFILES_COLUMNS_AND_APP_MAPPING.md`—use it when fixing sync or account repopulation.
- **Profile image:** **`POST /api/profile-image`** accepts a data URL, uploads to Storage bucket **`profile-images`**, then sets **`profiles.profile_image`** using the **service role** (after **`getAuthUser`** validates the JWT). Client PATCH/queue intentionally omit base64 blobs; persistence requires this upload path so **`GET /api/profile`** returns the URL after sign-in.
- **Admin client details (Orders vs Appointments):** Orders and Appointments tabs share the same card layout (flex, gap 12px), typography (Covered By Your Grace 16px for date, Futura PT Medium 10px/12px for title and secondary text, #EB1C24 / #808080), left 85×85 area (orders: product image + "N ITEMS"; appointments: APT placeholder only, no label below), status pill (height 15px, padding 0 6px, borderRadius 2px, Futura PT Medium 8px). Appointment time is offset with `translateY(-2px)`. Empty state: "NO APPOINTMENTS YET" matches "NO ORDERS YET" styling.
- **Frontal Slayer Admin Alignment Protocol (2026-07-06 — mandatory):** Applies **only** to the Frontal Slayer Admin Dashboard (`/admin/dashboard`, `/admin/clients`, `/admin/marketing`, etc.) — **not** customer pages (M84 Design DNA) · **not** Studio OS HQ (M83 EIA). Controlled alignment — **not** redesign. Every existing admin page is **protected/finalized** unless the founder **explicitly names** it. Section-level changes only when approved; canon reference pages never altered. Before work: identify page · sections · untouched areas · proposal · ask if unclear. Goal: visual **coherence**, not uniformity. Full text: **`docs/frontal-slayer/ADMIN_ALIGNMENT_PROTOCOL.md`** · Cursor rule **`.cursor/rules/frontal-slayer-admin-alignment.mdc`**.
- **Client profile BIRTHDAY row:** Add BIRTHDAY between EMAIL and PHONE. Display format "AUGUST 30, 1989". Fallback order: birthDate → birthMonth+birthDay+birthYear (MM/DD/YYYY) → birthMonth+birthDay (MM/DD) → birthDay only ("Day 15") → "—". See MEMORY 2025-02-28.
- **Main card responsive height:** For the single main content card (border, bg-white/60, backdrop-blur-sm, p-4, mb-2) on list/settings-style pages: use proportional scaling so the card keeps the same visual proportion across viewports. **Wishlist lists** uses `calc(100vh * 520 / 745)` (520px at 745px viewport height). **Account Payment** and **Account Shipping** use `minHeight: calc(100vh * 510 / 900)`. Other pages (Wishlist main, Shopping bag, Admin clients, Account settings, Account menu open) use viewport-minus-fixed (e.g. `calc(100vh - 270px)` or `calc(100dvh - 160px)`). See MEMORY 2025-02-28 (main card responsiveness).
- **Branch & deploy policy (user preference — critical):** Do **all** work on **`master`** only. **Never create** `cursor/*`, `feature/*`, or side branches. **After each completed task:** **`./scripts/agent-commit.sh --sync-only "message"`** — one commit + push; **`[sync-only]`** skips Vercel via **`scripts/vercel-should-build.sh`**. **"Deploy now"** → **`--deploy-now`** (Vercel build when account active). **Auto-append `MEMORY.md` after completed tasks (default ON).** **`preview/mobile` was deleted** — do not recreate.
- **Studio OS workspace bootstrap (public routes):** Do **not** top-level `import '../workspaces'` from modules loaded on every page (`App.tsx` → `AdminGuard`). **`AdminGuard`** is **auth-only** — no **`WorkspaceProvider`**, no workspace import on **`/admin/dashboard`**. **`AdminStudioWorkspaceGuard`** wraps **`/admin/studio/*`** + **`/admin/studio-os/*`**, **`await`s `ensureWorkspacesBootstrapped()`**, then mounts **`WorkspaceProvider`**. **Do not** auto-run Milestone 30–36 platform demo seeds on workspaces import — export **`bootstrapWorkspacesPlatform()`** and call from **`AdminStudioLayout`** only.
- **Executive Organization (M41):** `/admin/studio/executive-organization` — living leadership org (Founder → CoS → executives → departments → teams → workers). Executives operate as **one leadership team** coordinated by **Chief of Staff**; core in **`src/studio-os-core/executive-organization/`**; links from CoS workspace and Knowledge Graph.
- **Organizational Inheritance (M42):** `/admin/studio/organizational-inheritance` — foundational platform for inheriting organizational genetics (DNA layers, playbooks, executives, knowledge) when creating new companies. Inheritance wizard linked from Workspace Creation Engine; genetic blending, simulator, institutional library, ancestry/timeline, evolution tracking; marketplace architecture prepared (not implemented). Core in **`src/studio-os-core/organizational-inheritance/`**.
- **Strategy Engine (M43):** `/admin/studio/strategy-engine` — defines the game each company is playing; strategy board, profile, initiatives, strategic bets, alignment checks, health score, decision journal, reviews, simulation, strategy inheritance. Connected to CoS (prioritization), Newsroom (page strategy linkage), Leadership DNA, Organizational Inheritance, KG. Workspace profiles seeded for NDXBOOK + Frontal Slayer (reference data only — no FS code changes). Core in **`src/studio-os-core/strategy-engine/`**.
- **Campaign Engine (M44):** `/admin/studio/campaign-engine` — transforms strategy into coordinated **production pipelines**; deliverables are **Master Content Assets™** + platform derivatives (see **Master Content Pipeline™**). Campaign workspace, builder, deliverables (newsroom-linked), calendar, intelligence, analytics, health, experiments (Labs), retrospectives, playbooks, inheritance. Connected to Strategy Engine, Newsroom, CoS, Labs, KG. Core in **`src/studio-os-core/campaign-engine/`**.
- **Master Content Pipeline™ (2026-07-07 — product logic + UX architecture, not DR · not new milestone):** Permanent content operating philosophy — campaigns are **production pipelines**, not publishing pipelines. **Master Content Asset™** = single source of truth; pages/posts are derivatives. **17-stage lifecycle:** concept → campaign assignment → research → storyboard → talent → production planning → master creation → editing → Concierge Review Board™ → founder approval → Content Expansion Engine™ → multi-platform review → scheduling → publishing → performance → Studio Intelligence learning → Knowledge Library™. Core: **`src/studio-os-core/content-pipeline/`** (`lifecycle.ts` · `mapping.ts` · `concierge-review.ts` · `types.ts`) · UX **`MasterContentLifecycleStrip`** in Campaign Deliverables + NDXBook Page 001 pipeline · docs **`docs/studio-os/master-content-pipeline.md`**. Inherited by Campaign Engine · Newsroom · Publishing Studio · Knowledge Library · Studio Intelligence. NDXBook Page 001 = stage-7 pilot (`mapNdxbookPageToLifecycle`).
- **Master Content Pipeline — Lifecycle Gates (2026-07-07 — operating model upgrade, docs only):** Canonical content lifecycle promoted from Campaign Engine feature to **platform-wide operating model**. **Ten named gates:** DISCOVER · DEVELOP · ASSEMBLY · PRODUCTION · REVIEW · EXPANSION · APPROVAL · PUBLISH · MEASURE · LEARNING (entry/exit artifacts documented per gate). **System name unchanged:** Master Content Pipeline™. Products **consume** gates — Campaign Engine · Newsroom · Website Builder · Publishing Studio · Social Studio · Email Studio · future content products do not own independent workflows. Gate specs: **`docs/studio-os/master-content-pipeline-gates.md`**. Terminology: *"Page 001 is in Review Gate"* · *"Campaign 024 passed Approval Gate"*. Legacy 17-stage code registry preserved; docs and architecture use gate names as canonical. UI gate naming on future implementation pass.
- **Studio Production Engine™ (2026-07-07 — department UI shipped Page 001 pilot):** Implements Master Content Pipeline as **ten department workspaces** at `/admin/studio/ndxbook/newsroom/:departmentId`. See **`docs/studio-os/studio-production-engine.md`**. Lives **below** Creative Direction Studio™.
- **Creative Direction Studio™ (2026-07-07 — foundational creative subsystem):** Canonical **living creative brain** for every project — **above** Studio Production Engine (not a department). Continuous direction · Inspiration Library with Studio Intelligence extraction · Living Mood Board · parallel creative branches/timelines · natural-language Studio Orb commands · downstream impact warnings · Creative Direction Notes (Founder Notes evolution). Every department reads active direction before work. NDXBook pilot: **`/admin/studio/ndxbook/creative-direction`** · core **`src/studio-os-core/creative-direction-studio/`** · storage **`studioOsCreativeDirection_v1`** · docs **`docs/studio-os/creative-direction-studio.md`**. Foundational alongside Studio Orb · DLS · Component Catalog · Design Governance.
- **Living Creative Headquarters Experience™ (2026-07-07 — Experience DNA amendment):** Studio OS is **not** productivity software, a dashboard, or pages — founders run a **luxury creative headquarters** (The Movies / Sims / Watch Dogs / Xbox principles). **Roles:** Founder = Studio Director · Studio Orb = Executive Creative Director · Concierge = Department Head · Master Content Asset = project protagonist in transit. Departments = **buildings on the lot** · dispatch/handoff not forms. Core **`src/studio-os-core/experience-dna/`** (`departmentDestinations.ts` · mastery tiers · ambient arrival copy). UI: **`HeadquartersExperiencePanels`** · enhanced production lot strip. Docs **`docs/studio-os/living-creative-headquarters-experience.md`**. Permeates Creative Direction Studio · Studio Production Engine · all future products.
- **Studio Project™ (2026-07-07 — platform philosophy amendment):** Primary user-facing object — users **direct productions**, not pages. **Project** = complete creative initiative (direction · brief · mood board · assets · timeline · outputs). **Outputs** = linked derivatives (Reel · Landing Page · Newsletter · …). **Project Dashboard** = Mission Control health view. User-facing terminology: Project · Production · Output · Creative Direction · Production Timeline · Deliverable · Department · Mission Control — **not** Page · Post · File · Document · Screen · Task. Technical URLs/registry IDs unchanged (`page001`, `/admin/studio/ndxbook/newsroom`). Core **`src/studio-os-core/studio-project/`** · UI **`ProjectMissionControlDashboard`** · hook **`useStudioProjectDashboard`** · docs **`docs/studio-os/project-model.md`**. NDXBook pilot: Project 001 = Truth Tuesday · Credit Education.
- **Headquarters Engine™ (2026-07-07 — platform architecture amendment, docs only):** Studio OS stops thinking in **apps · templates · feature packs** — thinks in **living businesses**. Every customer owns a **Headquarters** that **grows** via **Headquarters Expansions™** (business capabilities: departments · workflows · AI specialists · concierges · automations · analytics · progression — not templates). **Headquarters Marketplace™** — creators sell **business architecture** (living operational systems), not graphics/page templates; **cross-industry** Expansion install encouraged. **Hierarchy:** Headquarters → Buildings → Departments → Workspaces → Projects → Assets → Tasks. **Vision:** world's first **immersive Business Headquarters Operating System** — founders **step inside their business**, not open software. **Game design philosophy:** meaningful progression (Sims/Movies/Watch Dogs/Xbox principles) — **not gamification**. Docs **`docs/studio-os/headquarters-engine.md`** · **`platform-vision.md`** · **`headquarters-marketplace.md`** · Master Spec **`core-philosophies.yaml` v1.2** (+5 philosophies). Expands M88 Expansion Center · M89 monetization language · reframes marketplace docs. **No implementation code** in this amendment.
- **Studio Department SDK™ (2026-07-07 — canonical engine spec, docs only):** Permanent foundation for **all** Studio OS departments — departments are **interactive worlds**, not pages/dashboards. **17-system SDK** at **`docs/studio-os/sdk/`** (anatomy · spatial layout · object library · interaction engine · AI employees · asset standard · visual/motion/audio language · Company Genome integration · department runtime · world routing · marketplace packaging · FAL asset compiler · Cursor runtime requirements · creation guide · QA checklist). **Rules:** modular assets only (never flattened scenes) · Company Genome™ injects all branding · FAL generates parts · Cursor assembles at runtime · physical interaction verbs (not form-first) · AI employees collaborate · marketplace-ready by default. Schema namespace **`studio.department.sdk.v1`**. **No React/UI implementation** in this sprint.
- **Studio Asset Compiler™ (2026-07-07 — core engine spec, docs only):** Canonical generation engine converting structured company data (Company Genome · Department DNA · Project Intent · Design Language · Experience DNA · World Rules) into modular **Department Asset Packages** for Studio Runtime. **15-doc engine** at **`docs/studio-os/engine/asset-compiler/`** (overview · input system · prompt compiler · generation pipeline · package spec · metadata · department compiler · genome injection · world assembly · versioning · regeneration · QA · marketplace export · AI provider abstraction · implementation guide). **14-doc manufacturing layer** at **`docs/studio-os/engines/studio-asset-compiler/`** (README · compiler-overview · compiler-flow · input-spec · output-spec · prompt-expansion-engine · generation-pipeline · dependency-resolution · quality-engine · package-schema · runtime-manifest · provider-abstraction · build-report-schema · future-roadmap) — **The Manufacturing Engine**: accepts official **Department Definition** (e.g. `departments/creative-direction-studio/`) → outputs **`DepartmentPackage.zip`** (`CreativeDirectionStudio_Package.zip`) with 16 folders (01_environment–16_preview) · `package-manifest.json` · `build-report.md` · expanded `13_prompts/` · Build Health score · 12-stage generation pipeline · provider-agnostic (FAL today). **Pipeline:** Definition → Adapt Genome/Room DNA → Expand prompts → Resolve dependencies → Quality Engine → Package. Consults **Studio Asset Registry™** for Smart Reuse before generation. **No implementation code** in these sprints.
- **Studio Asset Registry™ (2026-07-08 — canonical asset intelligence spec, docs only):** **The Living Library** — permanent creative memory and single source of truth for every reusable Studio OS resource (environment · furniture · materials · glass · lighting · VFX · audio · animations · cameras · UI · holograms · NPCs · concierges · Orb behaviors · icons · typography · brand themes · genome/room presets · department templates · prompt intelligence · interaction patterns · Marketplace Packs™). **14-doc engine** at **`docs/studio-os/engines/studio-asset-registry/`** (README · registry-overview · asset-schema · category-system · versioning · dependency-graph · reuse-engine · prompt-library · pack-support · company-genome-adaptation · search-system · runtime-integration · future-roadmap). **Registry Item** schema: ID · category · version · status · dependencies · genome/room compatibility · quality/performance scores · usage/revision history · licensing · pack ownership. **Smart Reuse:** Compiler asks Registry first (exist · adapt · inherit · merge · remix · upscale · evolve) — generation is last resort. **Absorbs Design Registry™** (`studio.design-registry.v1` → `studio.asset-registry.v1`). **Four-engine foundation:** Generator creates · Compiler manufactures · **Registry remembers** · Runtime operates. Cross-ref: Compiler · Generator · CDS golden department. **No implementation code** in this sprint.
