oads use **`wig-preview/{v}/NOIR/{hash}.webp`** (single combined asset per manifest row); the live color API caches **three angles** under **`wig-preview-live/{v}/NOIR/{colorTierHash}/{left|front|right}.webp`** where **`colorTierHash`** forces **`styling: NONE`** in the hash; **OFF BLACK** → **`OFF_BLACK`**; **JET BLACK** → **`JET_BLACK_OFF_BLACK`** (legacy Storage path) — so **pregenerated batch files do not satisfy** the live-color path; the API skips Fal only when those **live** objects exist. **Not** admin-email-gated; **all users** see committed/pending live WebPs when selecting options. **Customize draft vs hub:** On **`/build-a-wig/noir/customize/*`** sub-pages, WIP choices use **`customizeSelected*`** (and **`customizeSelectedHairStyling`** / **`customizeSelectedPartSelection`** for layers/part); **`selected*`** hub keys update on **Confirm** (or edit flow). Live preview **color** on steps **other than** **`.../customize/color`** resolves **`selectedColor`** first (confirmed), then **`customizeSelectedColor`** (draft); **`bawNoirLiveColorWigViewsPending`** applies only on the **color** sub-page. **Styling** and **hairline** NOIR customize sub-pages **persist `customizeSelected*` on every tap** (not only Back/Confirm) so preview resolution never falls back to stale **`selected*`** mid-draft. Exact **`/build-a-wig/noir/customize`** hub uses confirmed **`customizeSelected*`** only for live preview resolution — not in-flight draft taps. **NOIR color sub-page (`.../noir/customize/color`, `.../noir/edit/color`):** `resolveAdminNoirHubLiveWigViewsFromStorage` returns **only** color-tier live WebPs (`pending` + committed) — **not** salon/bangs styling triples — so swatch taps update the hero. Other NOIR step routes still composite styling/bangs when selected. Selecting a paid color **no longer clears** `bawNoirLiveColorWigViewsPending` before the next triple resolves — **optimistic** hash-based public URLs **first**, optional **single-`HEAD`** verify (`front.webp` only), then **`customStorageChange`**. The page **holds** the last good live triple in state while the next color resolves so the hero does **not** flash to naturals; **OFF BLACK** uses the **same** `wig-preview-live` Fal triples as other swatches (**not** forced static `/assets/` naturals — **`shouldUseCommittedBawNoirLiveColorWigViews`** includes **OFF BLACK**). **`POST /api/wig-preview/live-noir-color`:** any **signed-in** user may call — **missing** angles only unless **`forceRegenerate: true`** (re-runs Fal even when WebPs exist). **NOIR color** page: premium gate + **`liveWigViews`** drives the hero; Fal regen strip + **regen all** / **L-M-R** controls are **founder-only in the DOM** (`display: none`, `aria-hidden`) so text is not visible but tooling / parity with the old flow remains. **`POST /api/live-wig-after-color-styling`:** **`forceRegenerate`** is not founder-only (any signed-in session with Bearer for **new** Fal runs). If **`!forceRegenerate`** and all **`after-color/***` outputs already exist in Storage, the API returns **`publicUrls`** immediately (**`cacheOnly: true`**) **without** requiring **`Authorization`** — matches warm-cache styling preview when no Fal runs. **NOIR styling** page (`.../noir/edit/styling`, `.../noir/customize/styling`): live preview Fal calls use **`isPremiumMemberForGatedFeatures()`**; Fal / LIVE PREVIEW / regen **text** is **visible** on these routes only (still hidden on other NOIR BAW steps). **NOIR hairline** (`.../hairline`): founder hairline hint text shows only on these routes. **Showing** the Fal regen strip on **other** NOIR steps (styling regen, hairline hint, etc.) still requires **`isFounderNoirFalRegenUiVisible()`** — signed in **and** **`currentUser`** email is founder Gmail; other signed-in accounts never see those controls (they still see live WebPs from storage when applicable). Fal API still needs Bearer. **Live LAYERS / CRIMPS / FLAT IRON (after-color styling):** **`POST /api/live-wig-after-color-styling`*